From 6a97e112d1538529765e298c7c0b590a68d9268a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:58:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/66] sparc32: advertise the compare-and-swap trap in
 AT_HWCAP

A process that wants the kernel to perform a compare-and-swap has no way
to find out whether this kernel will do it.  Issuing the trap to find out
is not an option: on a kernel without it the trap is a bad trap and the
process dies.

This matters because the caller cannot decide from its own build either.
A binary built for pre-v9 has no compare-and-swap instruction and must ask
the kernel, but it may well be running on a kernel that predates the trap,
or on sparc64 in compat mode where the trap does not exist at all and a
32-bit process reads its hwcap word from elf_64.h.  In both cases it has
to do something else - whatever it can manage by itself, or report the
operation unsupported.  Note that a private lock is not a general answer:
it cannot make a word atomic against another process, which is the reason
for the trap in the first place.

Guessing is worse than dying, too.  On sparc64 ta 0x11 is not an illegal
instruction but the old 64-bit system call trap, so a process that issued
it there would make a wild syscall rather than take a signal.

Advertise it in AT_HWCAP so the question can be asked before it is too
late.  Bit 0x10000000 is unused on sparc32 and on sparc64, so it reads as
clear in exactly the cases where the trap is absent.  Reserve the same bit
in elf_64.h with a comment, so it is not handed to something else later
and mistaken for this by a 32-bit process running there.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_32.h | 10 +++++++++-
 arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_64.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_32.h b/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_32.h
index 37a6016c9ccd..7b0dca3f5160 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_32.h
+++ b/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_32.h
@@ -64,6 +64,13 @@
 #define HWCAP_SPARC_MULDIV      8
 #define HWCAP_SPARC_V9		16
 #define HWCAP_SPARC_ULTRA3	32
+/* The kernel performs a compare-and-swap on request; see
+   Documentation/arch/sparc/cas-trap.rst.  A caller that finds the bit clear
+   must not issue the trap - on sparc64, where a 32-bit process gets this word
+   from elf_64.h, that instruction is the old 64-bit system call - and has to
+   fall back to whatever it can do itself, or report the operation
+   unsupported.  */
+#define HWCAP_SPARC_CASTRAP	0x10000000
 
 #define CORE_DUMP_USE_REGSET
 
@@ -121,7 +128,8 @@ typedef struct {
 
 /* Most sun4m's have them all.  */
 #define ELF_HWCAP	(HWCAP_SPARC_FLUSH | HWCAP_SPARC_STBAR | \
-			 HWCAP_SPARC_SWAP | HWCAP_SPARC_MULDIV)
+			 HWCAP_SPARC_SWAP | HWCAP_SPARC_MULDIV | \
+			 HWCAP_SPARC_CASTRAP)
 
 /* This yields a string that ld.so will use to load implementation
    specific libraries for optimization.  This is more specific in
diff --git a/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_64.h b/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_64.h
index 694ed081cf8d..950521c92194 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_64.h
+++ b/arch/sparc/include/asm/elf_64.h
@@ -98,6 +98,8 @@
  */
 #define HWCAP_SPARC_CRYPTO	0x04000000 /* CRYPTO insns available */
 #define HWCAP_SPARC_ADI		0x08000000 /* ADI available */
+/* 0x10000000 is HWCAP_SPARC_CASTRAP on sparc32 and must stay clear here: a
+   32-bit process reads this word too, and there is no such trap on sparc64.  */
 
 #define CORE_DUMP_USE_REGSET
 
